WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:04.800
GrowthOps OS. Ad platforms, the CRM and the bank each report a different revenue figure. Which one is right?

2
00:00:05.250 --> 00:00:12.300
Ad platforms claim $3.72M. The CRM books $3.32M. The bank collected $3.06M. Which number is right?

3
00:00:12.750 --> 00:00:19.800
Every step from CRM bookings to cash is computed, so nothing is left unexplained: the residual is $0.

4
00:00:20.250 --> 00:00:26.800
Meta reports 7.3× return on ad spend. On the cash the business actually kept, it is 3.3×.

5
00:00:27.250 --> 00:00:35.300
Lead quality fell from 29.8% to 20.4%. The detector caught it within three days and traced 92% of the drop to one new campaign.

6
00:00:35.750 --> 00:00:41.300
That campaign, meta_broad_v17, lifted leads 61% while their quality fell.

7
00:00:41.750 --> 00:00:49.300
A seven-page Power BI report generated from a specification, with 215 documented DAX measures. This summary is written in DAX.

8
00:00:49.750 --> 00:00:57.300
The Excel workbook is formulas over the same dbt marts, and reaches the same answer on its own: $309,900 net cash, as in Power BI.

9
00:00:57.750 --> 00:01:05.800
Tests hold every claim: both bridges tie exactly, the detector finds each planted incident, and the workbook reconciles.

10
00:01:06.250 --> 00:01:12.300
Download the workbook and compare it with the Power BI report. A fictional business on generated data, with problems planted on purpose so the analysis can be scored.

